## 1. NEW BUSINESS ALERT
==============================================

### Competitors
- **Company Search UK** — Paid company data reports (£5-20 each)
- **DueDil** — Company intelligence for enterprises (expensive)
- **Endole** — Business data platform (£99+/mo)
- **Local data resellers** — Sell lists of new companies (£200-500 one-off)

### What They Do Well
- Deep company profiles with financial data
- Credit scores and risk assessment
- Historical data going back years

### Where They Fall Short
- Focus on CREDIT CHECKS and due diligence, not LEAD GENERATION
- Expensive (£99-500/mo) for what you need
- No daily email alerts for new companies
- No CRM integration or simple lead delivery

### How We Beat Them
| Factor | Competitors | New Business Alert |
|--------|-------------|-------------------|
| Price | £99-500/mo | £97/mo |
| Focus | Credit checking | Lead generation |
| Delivery | Portal access | Daily email |
| Filters | Company type only | Area + type + date |
| Simplicity | Complex dashboards | One email, that's it |

### Value Props To Lead With
- "Know every new business in your area within 24 hours"
- "Accountants charge £500+ for a year's service. One client pays for our whole year."
- "Web designers: new businesses need websites. We tell you when they register."
- "Available in CSV or daily email — whichever you prefer"

