## 3. PROBATE LEADS
==============================================

### Competitors
- **TwentyCi / MoverAlerts** — Enterprise property data (£300-500/mo)
- **Land Registry Direct** — Free but manual (£3 per search)
- **Probate data resellers** — Small niche providers (£200-500/mo)
- **Legal databases** — Expensive legal reference tools

### What They Do Well
- Land Registry is the authoritative source (but manual and per-search cost)
- TwentyCi has comprehensive data (but overkill and expensive)

### Where They Fall Short
- Land Registry: You have to search manually, no alerts, £3 per search adds up
- TwentyCi: Enterprise pricing, too expensive for small firms
- No dedicated probate lead service at an affordable price

### How We Beat Them
| Factor | Land Registry | TwentyCi | Probate Leads |
|--------|--------------|----------|---------------|
| Price | £3/search | £300-500/mo | £247/mo |
| Delivery | Manual | Daily email | Daily email + CSV |
| Coverage | You search | National | National |
| Setup | None needed | Phone call needed | Instant |
| Exclusivity | No | No | Per area available |

### Value Props To Lead With
- "Every probate grant means a property to sell, a house to clear, or an estate to manage."
- "Estate agents: probate properties are motivated sellers. Contact them before the listing."
- "Solicitors: families dealing with probate need legal help. Be the first firm they call."
- "£247/mo is less than 10 single Land Registry searches — and we search every single day."
- "One probate instruction pays for 6 months of subscription."

